"""OPT-125M -> Relax -> DistIR (TP=4), showcase style.

Same shape as the TVM website flow: torch.export -> from_exported_program ->
passes. The only extra step is that DistIR needs three things the importer
cannot know, so they are attached programmatically after import:

  1. module attr  "device_num"
  2. global info  "mesh"
  3. annotate_sharding on the column-parallel weights (q/k/v/fc1)

Everything else (out_proj, fc2 -> row-parallel, and the two allreduces) is
inferred by PropagateSharding. That inference is the thing under test.

Why OPT-125M: activation is ReLU (already in propagate_sharding.cc
unary_op_names), q/k/v are separate nn.Linear so no `split` is needed, learned
positional embeddings so no rotary, and MHA not GQA. fp32 because cpuccl's
allreduce rejects fp16/bf16 (cpuccl.cc:86-98 ReduceBytes).
"""


